# Vercel environment — `deploy/vercel` branch

Copy these into Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables. Values
marked **build** are inlined into the browser bundle; change them only by
redeploying. Values marked **request** are read by `vercel.json` routes.

```dotenv
# ---- build: public browser config -----------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY
NEXT_PUBLIC_WORKBENCH_ENABLED=true
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.vercel.app

# ---- request: compute gateway ---------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the Kaggle tunnel (scheme + host only, no /api suffix).
# A named tunnel keeps this stable; a quick tunnel changes on every restart.
KAGGLE_ORIGIN=https://YOUR_TUNNEL_HOST

# Must equal the KELASKA_PROXY_TOKEN secret on the Kaggle notebook.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
KAGGLE_PROXY_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_A_LONG_RANDOM_VALUE

# ---- request: on-demand Kaggle wake (the single Vercel function) --------
# The auth provider calls POST /api/wake when the tunnel has no backend.
# Kaggle credentials stay on Vercel; the kernel's own app secrets stay in
# Kaggle Secrets (KELASKA_ENV_B64, KELASKA_AUTH_PUBLIC_URL,
# KELASKA_APP_TUNNEL_TOKEN, KELASKA_PROXY_TOKEN, KELASKA_GITHUB_TOKEN).
KAGGLE_USERNAME=YOUR_KAGGLE_USERNAME
KAGGLE_KEY=YOUR_KAGGLE_API_KEY_OR_KGAT_TOKEN
# Full owner/kernel-slug ref. Create this kernel once with the secrets above.
KAGGLE_KERNEL_REF=akjdev/kelaska-app
# Defaults to deploy/kaggle/kelaska-vercel-kernel.py on the deploy/kaggle branch.
KAGGLE_KERNEL_SOURCE_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ade-karya/KelasKA/refs/heads/deploy/kaggle/deploy/kaggle/kelaska-vercel-kernel.py
KAGGLE_KERNEL_TITLE=KelasKA Compute
# Only used when POST /api/wake is called with {"gpu": true}; otherwise the
# kernel starts CPU-only (no weekly GPU quota consumed).
KAGGLE_MACHINE_SHAPE=NvidiaTeslaT4
KAGGLE_SESSION_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=42000
# GPU-only session (started by POST /api/wake {"gpu": true}) runs beside the
# CPU app: separate kernel, tunnel and domain.
KAGGLE_GPU_KERNEL_REF=akjdev/kelaska-gpu-worker
KELASKA_GPU_TUNNEL_TOKEN=YOUR_GPU_TUNNEL_TOKEN
KELASKA_GPU_PUBLIC_URL=https://gpu.kelaska.riau.ai
```

`SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `DATABASE_URL`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`, `AUTH_SECRET`
and every other server secret stay on **Kaggle**, in `KELASKA_ENV_B64`. Never add
them here — the static bundle is public.

Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs must contain
`https://YOUR_PROJECT.vercel.app/api/auth/supabase/callback` exactly. With
accounts on, the Kaggle app's `AUTH_PUBLIC_URL` must be the same Vercel origin;
otherwise Google sign-in redirects to the tunnel host after the callback.
